From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bpereira <bpereira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 19:03:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Align caption margin adjustments for Taffy's tagged pointers

A caption margin adjustment is handed to Taffy as a calc() pointer, and Taffy's CompactLength keeps its tag in the pointer's low three bits. On wasm32 the struct only asked for 4-byte alignment, which held only because dlmalloc rounds every chunk to 8; an allocator that honours the requested alignment failed Taffy's assertion and panicked during table layout.

Signed-off-by: bpereira <bpereira@cloudflare.com>
---
 src/layout/table.rs | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/layout/table.rs b/src/layout/table.rs
index 947f154..c6638b5 100644
--- a/src/layout/table.rs
+++ b/src/layout/table.rs
@@ -65,7 +65,10 @@ pub struct TableContext {
     caption_margin_adjustments: Vec<Arc<CaptionMarginAdjustment>>,
 }

+// Taffy's CompactLength keeps a tag in the low three bits of a calc pointer, and this is passed
+// as one, so it must be 8-aligned on 32-bit targets too rather than relying on the allocator.
 #[derive(Debug)]
+#[repr(align(8))]
 struct CaptionMarginAdjustment {
     value: taffy::LengthPercentageAuto,
     spacing: f32,
